{
  "title": "Sequences and melody",
  "startSide": "back",
  "learned": [
    "A clock moves a sequencer step by step",
    "Gate for the rhythm, CV for the pitch (1 V per octave)",
    "A quantizer keeps every note in a scale",
    "Length, rests and random notes"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "A sequencer plays a row of voltages one after another, in time with a clock. Your voice from lesson 3 is in the rack (the trill is unplugged), with three new modules: a sequencer, a quantizer and a random source. Let's give the voice a melody.",
      "done": {
        "next": true
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Patch X2 of the clock to CLOCK of the sequencer. The sequencer now moves one step on every eighth note.",
      "side": "back",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Clock",
          "output": "x2"
        },
        {
          "module": "SEQ",
          "input": "Clock"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "cable": {
          "from": {
            "module": "Clock",
            "output": "x2"
          },
          "to": {
            "module": "SEQ",
            "input": "Clock"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Patch GATE of the sequencer to GATE of the envelope (the clock's cable goes). You hear one note per step, all at the same pitch.",
      "side": "back",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "SEQ",
          "output": "Gate"
        },
        {
          "module": "ADSR",
          "input": "Gate"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "cable": {
          "from": {
            "module": "SEQ",
            "output": "Gate"
          },
          "to": {
            "module": "ADSR",
            "input": "Gate"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Patch CV of the sequencer to V/OCT of the oscillator. One volt more is one octave higher, so the step voltages now set the pitch.",
      "side": "back",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "SEQ",
          "output": "CV"
        },
        {
          "module": "VCO",
          "input": "V/Oct"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "cable": {
          "from": {
            "module": "SEQ",
            "output": "CV"
          },
          "to": {
            "module": "VCO",
            "input": "V/Oct"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Press Tab and turn the knobs of steps 1 and 3. Each knob is the pitch of its step. Most positions sound out of tune: the knobs are smooth, notes are not.",
      "side": "front",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "SEQ",
          "param": "Step 1 CV"
        },
        {
          "module": "SEQ",
          "param": "Step 3 CV"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "all": [
          {
            "param": {
              "module": "SEQ",
              "param": "Step 1 CV"
            },
            "moved": 0.1
          },
          {
            "param": {
              "module": "SEQ",
              "param": "Step 3 CV"
            },
            "moved": 0.1
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "A quantizer snaps any voltage to the nearest note of a scale. Press Tab, patch CV of the sequencer to the V/OCT input of the quantizer, and its V/OCT output to V/OCT of the oscillator (the old cable goes).",
      "side": "back",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "SEQ",
          "output": "CV"
        },
        {
          "module": "Quantizer",
          "input": "V/Oct"
        },
        {
          "module": "Quantizer",
          "output": "V/Oct"
        },
        {
          "module": "VCO",
          "input": "V/Oct"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "all": [
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "SEQ",
                "output": "CV"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "Quantizer",
                "input": "V/Oct"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "Quantizer",
                "output": "V/Oct"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "VCO",
                "input": "V/Oct"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Press Tab and turn SCALE of the quantizer. Every knob position now lands on a note of the scale, so any setting sounds musical.",
      "side": "front",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Quantizer",
          "param": "Scale"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "param": {
          "module": "Quantizer",
          "param": "Scale"
        },
        "moved": 0.01
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Turn LENGTH of the sequencer. The sequence now repeats after fewer steps: three or five steps against the beat make a pattern that shifts.",
      "side": "front",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "SEQ",
          "param": "Length"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "param": {
          "module": "SEQ",
          "param": "Length"
        },
        "moved": 0.1
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Click the gate button of step 2 to switch it off. The step keeps its pitch but sends no gate: a rest.",
      "side": "front",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "SEQ",
          "param": "Step 2 gate"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "param": {
          "module": "SEQ",
          "param": "Step 2 gate"
        },
        "max": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Now let chance write the melody. Press Tab, patch X2 of the clock to CLOCK of the random module, and STEP of the random module to the V/OCT input of the quantizer (instead of the sequencer).",
      "side": "back",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Clock",
          "output": "x2"
        },
        {
          "module": "Random",
          "input": "Clock"
        },
        {
          "module": "Random",
          "output": "Step"
        },
        {
          "module": "Quantizer",
          "input": "V/Oct"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "all": [
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "Clock",
                "output": "x2"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "Random",
                "input": "Clock"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "Random",
                "output": "Step"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "Quantizer",
                "input": "V/Oct"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Clock, sequencer or random voltage, quantizer, voice: that is how most modular melodies are made. The sequencer still plays the rhythm through its gates. Press Next to finish.",
      "done": {
        "next": true
      }
    }
  ]
}
